  "tag_ids": [],
  "policy_sha256": "84f656b16099dcb248866f714453e5bd3e275bdb5d4929c4fad838ee8b29ed2c",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "gv-729347-b00001",
      "text": "Facebook users have been outraged by the social networking giant's blocking of news stories in Australia. The ongoing dispute between Facebook and the Australian government came to a head on February 18, 2021, when the platform blocked news over a draft code of conduct concerning payment for news content.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 1,
      "body_start": 0,
      "body_end": 306,
      "source_links": [
        "https://globalvoices.org/2020/09/18/australian-government-on-collision-course-with-facebook-and-google-over-news-revenue/"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-729347-b00002",
      "text": "The legislation drafted by the Australian government “would force tech giants Facebook and Google to negotiate with media companies over payment for linking to their news stories.” BBC News has a useful summary of the dispute so far.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 2,
      "body_start": 308,
      "body_end": 541,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.bbc.com/news/world-australia-56116738"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-729347-b00003",
      "text": "#DeleteFacebook and #BoycottZuckerberg were just two of the trending hashtags on Twitter. “Paul” might have only 25 followers but he summed up a common reaction:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 3,
      "body_start": 543,
      "body_end": 704,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-729347-b00004",
      "text": "The Facebook ban was far-reaching. Australian publishers could not share or post news. International publishers could not be viewed or shared Down Under. The Aussie community could not view or share Australian or international news content or pages. The international community could not view or share Australian news content on Facebook or content from Australian news pages.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 4,
      "body_start": 706,
      "body_end": 1082,
      "source_links": [
        "https://about.fb.com/news/2021/02/changes-to-sharing-and-viewing-news-on-facebook-in-australia/"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-729347-b00005",
      "text": "As might be expected, the mainstream media were very displeased. The Age newspaper’s front page was typical:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 5,
      "body_start": 1084,
      "body_end": 1192,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-729347-b00006",
      "text": "Facebook raised the stakes when it “inadvertently” blocked non-news sites such as The Bureau of Meteorology, emergency services, health pages and a host of other community services. The response was stinging:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 6,
      "body_start": 1194,
      "body_end": 1402,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-729347-b00007",
      "text": "Many brought into the discussion the impact on the already marginalised, such as indigenous communities:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 7,
      "body_start": 1404,
      "body_end": 1508,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-729347-b00008",
      "text": "Facebook blamed the Australian government’s definition of news content for the bungle and started reversing these “inadvertent” blocks. Some Aussies agreed:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 8,
      "body_start": 1510,
      "body_end": 1666,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/feb/18/facebook-condemned-in-uk-and-us-for-attempt-to-bully-democracy"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-729347-b00009",
      "text": "Despite the strident attacks on Facebook by his government, the Australian federal treasurer, Josh Frydenberg, maintained that negotiations were continuing on the implementation of its draft code. Perhaps he could follow the lead of the United Kingdom, where Facebook News began rolling out last month.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 9,
      "body_start": 1668,
      "body_end": 1970,
      "source_links": [
        "https://theguardian.com/technology/2020/dec/01/facebook-to-pay-uk-media-millions-to-licence-news-stories",
        "https://www.abc.net.au/news/2021-02-19/frydenberg-zuckerberg-meeting-news-media-facebook-ban/13171120",
        "https://www.cnbc.com/2021/01/26/facebook-starts-rolling-out-facebook-news-to-uk-users.html"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-729347-b00010",
      "text": "One source of “news” that has not been blocked is the satirical website The Chaser, which has several stories about the policy brawl including this one:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 10,
      "body_start": 1972,
      "body_end": 2124,
      "source_links": [
        "https://chaser.com.au/news"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-729347-b00011",
      "text": "Some online believe that the government is more than happy to have a major dispute to take attention away from the scandal revolving around an alleged rape in parliament house:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 11,
      "body_start": 2126,
      "body_end": 2302,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.abc.net.au/news/2021-02-19/scott-morrison-office-faces-questions-over-brittany-higgins/13171252"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-729347-b00012",
      "text": "Another concern has been that the absence of reputable news stories may lead to the dominance misinformation and disinformation on the platform:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 12,
      "body_start": 2304,
      "body_end": 2448,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-729347-b00013",
      "text": "Some see large media organisations as the source of much of the misinformation:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 13,
      "body_start": 2450,
      "body_end": 2529,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-729347-b00014",
      "text": "At Techdirt, Mike Masnick has a detailed defence of Facebook's position on the code:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 14,
      "body_start": 2531,
      "body_end": 2615,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.techdirt.com/articles/20210217/22383446265/bizarre-reaction-to-facebooks-decision-to-get-out-news-business-australia.shtml?s=09"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-729347-b00015",
      "text": "> This fight was not “Facebook v. Australia.” Or “Facebook v. journalism” even though some ignorant or dishonest people are making it out to be the case. This was always “Rupert Murdoch v. the open web.” We may not like Facebook in the role of the defender of the open web (and it's far from the best representative for the open web).",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 15,
      "body_start": 2617,
      "body_end": 2951,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "blockquote",
      "source_is_quotation": true
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-729347-b00016",
      "text": "Jeff Jarvis from the City University of New York made similar arguments on Buzzmachine. It includes this interview with ABC TV News Australia:",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 16,
      "body_start": 2953,
      "body_end": 3095,
      "source_links": [
        "https://buzzmachine.com/2021/02/18/murdochs-law-and-the-net/"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-729347-b00017",
      "text": "Meanwhile, Google has made considerable progress in its response to the proposed legislation. The threatened removal of its search engine in Australia is increasingly unlikely. A number of deals have been made, including one with Rupert Murdoch’s News Corp, to pay for content in its Google News Showcase.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 17,
      "body_start": 3097,
      "body_end": 3402,
      "source_links": [
        "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2021/feb/17/news-corp-agrees-deal-with-google-over-payments-for-journalism"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-729347-b00018",
      "text": "In a fitting twist they, apparently briefly, blocked their own page.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 18,
      "body_start": 3404,
      "body_end": 3472,
      "source_links": [
        "https://gizmodo.com/facebook-accidentally-blocks-own-page-in-australia-foll-1846294300"
      ],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gv-729347-b00019",
      "text": "Perhaps Facebook should take a warning from the fact that the issue was no longer trending on Twitter the next day.",
      "page": null,
      "paragraph": 19,
      "body_start": 3474,
      "body_end": 3589,
      "source_links": [],
      "source_kind": "p",
      "source_is_quotation": false
    }
  ],
